# Every text file stays LF in the working tree, on Windows too.
#
# `bin` is src/index.ts and it starts with a shebang. A clone on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true would turn that line into "#!/usr/bin/env node<CR>", and a
# publish from that clone ships it: macOS and Linux then look for an interpreter
# named "node\r" and the command dies with a message about a bad interpreter.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
